#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115124 :question/id #uuid "cd56314d-f45a-55be-9762-983fe507a1a0" :question/math-academy-id "e-6173" :question/problem "Given the system\n![](images/0e/0e89fc57b6af2ddf2a71246dbadc7feb8425d1e1e0ab8f988e7e8ad97d22cff7.svg)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/3e/3e3e8adb0d6e13f7d3b4c3e450b25a789480ac53189ab92385174688e460b2cc.svg)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/41/4122fb4ef56aa99161b15bc25001ca728a6cf7dae36d5dac0aac9b03dc411685.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/math-academy-id 493 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f8ae27a-136e-5076-9ed6-6bf54a2fc555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300191} {:answer/id #uuid "54c660e7-e22a-5936-aedc-8d1501ef6251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300399} {:answer/id #uuid "78c68ded-4a4c-55f8-9c3a-af0dfcb92412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300555} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee5558c-7494-5c81-a3c3-c047093a1f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300590} {:answer/id #uuid "d300d0ee-b9ac-5fd6-a739-ac93cb542fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ee5558c-7494-5c81-a3c3-c047093a1f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300590} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4cd364f-a7b0-5f37-96dd-39259066615e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301867}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "402ab26a-a0df-5fc5-a264-b91a4c6d7d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-32242" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -x+2y=6 \\\\  & 2x-3y=13 \\\\  & 5x-y=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system has a unique solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 75\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f9fc63-1e5b-58f3-9165-48ecf337098a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324140} {:answer/id #uuid "6531f6ef-7836-5c36-8ad2-b64340ef2dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324806} {:answer/id #uuid "716e8f1f-3359-5b9c-a2b5-8043eda079e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324907} {:answer/id #uuid "942d2637-f186-5cc3-808c-b7d930c541bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325234} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ddd36b-c315-54de-90f4-9ca1832ae646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "942d2637-f186-5cc3-808c-b7d930c541bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325234} :answer-field/id #uuid "715194d1-fad4-5aa4-83e8-d5906bffa1a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326421}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e80c83a9-9107-528b-af57-73287d15e8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42061" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48dd525f-5280-5616-ad30-ba5ee70ca286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263627} {:answer/id #uuid "97fe1cbb-75ac-5ed4-8c6f-28135d822617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264306} {:answer/id #uuid "9866ac27-4d10-5e12-a5f2-20a090920029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264310} {:answer/id #uuid "a4052d0a-62cc-5175-8982-a3a60adc8f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264396} {:answer/id #uuid "f78545d9-aee6-50ba-a9e2-99bc93090923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48dd525f-5280-5616-ad30-ba5ee70ca286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263627} :answer-field/id #uuid "63032b45-ca95-5403-83e8-7551c5787d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265418}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7e2bc11-b1bf-5938-9267-7923a80ec463" :question/math-academy-id "q-131719" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x+8y=-2 \\\\  & -3x-12y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is inconsistent\n\nII. The system is consistent dependent\n\nIII. The system has a unique solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2373407a-5dc4-5aa0-9261-b3a83be143a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263310} {:answer/id #uuid "37e5535a-47db-5120-b920-f8711ded0365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263504} {:answer/id #uuid "7e4a05dd-9346-5c44-8eaf-7488e248aafc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264090} {:answer/id #uuid "d7113481-5195-5749-9632-d40d020970ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264873} {:answer/id #uuid "f87a25e5-0907-579e-b6ce-cc2aa703c11e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e4a05dd-9346-5c44-8eaf-7488e248aafc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264090} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c27f11-9954-5e36-8021-98da12eda34a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265384}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a61d7528-3ce2-5d0a-af23-11395074997a" :question/math-academy-id "q-131723" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+z=3 \\\\  & -3x+3y-3z=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=19,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46470091-2ac4-5f59-adc5-0a311982854f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263616} {:answer/id #uuid "80d5d80a-e41d-5438-a1c7-07302fd289ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264107} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bfe79b-ea64-5a96-b000-a996d4345dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264709} {:answer/id #uuid "ce229d18-324f-56e3-9d1d-7ca1417d2702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264803} {:answer/id #uuid "d90f70d7-fb30-5e3a-a741-ee1cb5651f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3bfe79b-ea64-5a96-b000-a996d4345dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264709} :answer-field/id #uuid "7601e031-d2c6-5fed-a0f8-b45602534fa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265449}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09e95d08-30a6-5777-a8a8-348db8bfab42" :question/math-academy-id "q-131724" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=2 \\\\  & -3x-4y=3 \\\\  & 2x-4y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is inconsistent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-5,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31782fc1-be3a-570b-83a4-6a253ceacbe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342654} {:answer/id #uuid "49cbd863-e93c-5db8-869b-809f678b3040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342845} {:answer/id #uuid "99a2377c-7d5c-50a2-9c01-dffd06f0e462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343588} {:answer/id #uuid "b57d65ad-ebfa-5f7c-b1f8-4c03118d3947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343829} {:answer/id #uuid "b7aa2865-0c50-5f22-80eb-6161f09775ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99a2377c-7d5c-50a2-9c01-dffd06f0e462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343588} :answer-field/id #uuid "4da73cdd-da21-5939-a610-458af60d2aec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344624}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edc80b1b-d469-5071-b24d-3c90bb47fce6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74635" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -2x+4y+3z=0 \\\\  & x+3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & \\frac{3}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means that  we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01308e53-b92a-5d41-8e41-3edcada2f882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342256} {:answer/id #uuid "1c251f13-a18e-56fb-b700-41d13ecaa3bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342477} {:answer/id #uuid "b0020fb9-0863-546c-95a8-236e93a1dd5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343785} {:answer/id #uuid "c309108b-fd3a-5760-8a95-009d5ec4b565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343955} {:answer/id #uuid "d75038c3-3bd3-5a22-8af1-6c84cbbc8269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c251f13-a18e-56fb-b700-41d13ecaa3bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342477} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cccc34-d274-5062-9c39-f9e811dad04c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344805}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0089d19-a4b5-5ec4-beaa-917a294458ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-74637" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=-1 \\\\  & x-2y=1 \\\\  & -x-5y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 7y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-\\frac{3}{7}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{3}{7})=1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \nSo, we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70fce1c7-e3a4-581f-a7f2-a1059de561df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363110} {:answer/id #uuid "0cfa8239-78c8-5606-b95f-139c77f86daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363111} {:answer/id #uuid "980f588f-017e-5c7f-95ca-16cdf5340620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363112} {:answer/id #uuid "60a98dd7-9463-5196-915d-fdbc47f4c896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363113} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8c5afc-5d86-5fdd-9e84-6ad909f6e016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70fce1c7-e3a4-581f-a7f2-a1059de561df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363110} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fc17a8e-161a-5378-b587-a239e8268f84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8de2435-5f56-5017-bf79-0b535c719854" :question/math-academy-id "q-131718" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=2 \\\\  & -2x+7y+2z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d246db5c-17af-532c-91f0-d8c40fd97f95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364367} {:answer/id #uuid "b048bb21-9fa8-5eb6-91f1-1196c7642208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364368} {:answer/id #uuid "cc1a91fa-096c-500b-97f7-6683d89a1c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364369} {:answer/id #uuid "b785c74c-0a6c-5059-b07a-aacf6cdbcbed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364370} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c9f901-aed9-59d4-a3e1-fdcf34941998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9c9f901-aed9-59d4-a3e1-fdcf34941998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364371} :answer-field/id #uuid "696397bb-ae70-544b-a77e-b687e2fb2700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35b0295d-1e16-59cc-a201-696e791e0b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74643" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=8 \\\\  & x+y=-2 \\\\  & x+\\frac{1}{2}y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y=-2 \\\\ -y=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400632 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "461eef6c-aefb-5663-8d03-db54f697d105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400634} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d3c662-b67b-5b81-a307-d2b8efde6388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400635} {:answer/id #uuid "fbcd7fd9-5df8-5756-a9f3-48cc31c9e67e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400636} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9dcc22-2e73-56c0-825d-9e630c431eb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400637} {:answer/id #uuid "56e99c2d-29cc-5ded-a5f5-80ae572f982d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbcd7fd9-5df8-5756-a9f3-48cc31c9e67e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400636} :answer-field/id #uuid "97478289-921c-5024-949c-f21308c68969" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400633}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd791ebf-f827-5528-ae25-d3ac1f74c5cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-131720" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-6y-2z=4 \\\\  & 3x-9y-3z=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\nII. The system has no solution\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400639 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baed0cbf-38ec-5d81-9809-43dafa9379a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400641} {:answer/id #uuid "586150d0-53a3-501e-a821-68c180a394cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400642} {:answer/id #uuid "a39c1a3e-21c9-5508-8921-b8a05957b672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400643} {:answer/id #uuid "2247b748-8cef-53eb-82f9-2487685f5057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400644} {:answer/id #uuid "77d955a7-8c55-5d69-9764-f442198cee4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586150d0-53a3-501e-a821-68c180a394cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400642} :answer-field/id #uuid "62ec4d2b-adce-53b9-bdc4-0b08d9bbcf9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400640}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9b47374-5548-52b6-9b51-17d923fcd37b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131721" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+7y=1 \\\\  & -2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\nII. The system has no solution\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c927d7e-5c4b-5882-8721-adc2b5fd92e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400648} {:answer/id #uuid "64d69900-4157-5d22-aa0e-f4d914c8f721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400649} {:answer/id #uuid "2aba7c87-fdf8-526c-bf60-804628ebce56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400650} {:answer/id #uuid "fea224bb-b24d-5ae7-9e7c-a1698eef7494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400651} {:answer/id #uuid "a62e5405-e20d-5e9c-833b-ebb37c50b5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a62e5405-e20d-5e9c-833b-ebb37c50b5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400652} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb13c3f2-95da-5f1e-8dd8-8f023abfea3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400647}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-131722" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\nII. The system is consistent independent\nIII. The system has no solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7491008-5478-588e-9bdf-48009d63a5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402765} {:answer/id #uuid "0607f788-e8dd-5afc-8e48-6680586a38a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402766} {:answer/id #uuid "951d0cc3-a376-5df6-b506-f8d06e026e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402767} {:answer/id #uuid "c704cb2f-5ab2-5641-80d9-7f7e3a1c1a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402768} {:answer/id #uuid "642ef1b2-107b-5ded-a6cc-753b6bacad13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "951d0cc3-a376-5df6-b506-f8d06e026e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402767} :answer-field/id #uuid "90bdc196-1505-53d0-9a20-efa1ed00a2e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402764}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a930b2a-2578-5145-8e40-06b6cab16ba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42020" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+y=3 \\\\  & -2x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\nII. The system has a unique solution\nIII. The system is inconsistent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=2,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9541786-a906-58e9-a152-185ff736eaa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403789} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb03056-50c5-5118-adbd-9eed619e27a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403790} {:answer/id #uuid "735a983f-bd94-50e7-8c94-79524d3dc890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403791} {:answer/id #uuid "1f61f036-cb15-5c0c-9077-194388e6d6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403792} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a62366-a32a-5255-9a90-55ea9e42bab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "735a983f-bd94-50e7-8c94-79524d3dc890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403791} :answer-field/id #uuid "f91e44eb-099d-52c4-a904-f2a31b9b0fa8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403788}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8971116-e24d-5808-9b29-a50e168511e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74634" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=-1 \\\\  & 2x-4y=3 \\\\  & x+y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\n\nII. The system has a unique solution\n\nIII. The system is inconsistent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."}] :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115390 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114970 :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048932 :topic/math-academy-id 278 :topic/title "The Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999 :topic/math-academy-id 4139 :topic/title "Differentiating Vector-Valued Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245c1016-9019-52b2-a26a-6ac0bf1d16f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302689} {:answer/id #uuid "3f808494-9cca-5881-91d6-e03f7e4beb4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302855} {:answer/id #uuid "c25a159b-0633-5804-97a2-dac583cb6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc6f526-3686-5eb6-a589-7d892e3678c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303726} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d545bc-df18-5895-b155-25b6a18a659c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25a159b-0633-5804-97a2-dac583cb6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644} :answer-field/id #uuid "41acddb3-3570-5655-ad47-cf8c72851a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304257}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17db3926-f364-5101-a69e-c1d34df6ed10" :question/math-academy-id "q-33122" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad37ff22-26f6-50cd-9218-b742d80d0369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8, 1,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113623} {:answer/id #uuid "dce955db-803a-5eaa-8f40-9514713111b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12, 0, 48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113624} {:answer/id #uuid "51ccd42e-d655-5177-a52d-935b7434f13b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24, 3, 36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113625} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3be7aa-7f8b-5864-bdec-850462bcfb32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6, 0, 24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113626} {:answer/id #uuid "7a69da90-0384-583a-882a-0121d8fd94a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12, 3,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113627}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2b7ff49b-47bd-5f8b-a647-fae948868913" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113622}] :question/id #uuid "a73b3659-30e4-5063-9479-5d3e2f941065" :question/math-academy-id "q-33143" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$h(t)|= ⟨2t^{2}, t - 3, 8 + t^{3}⟩; g(t)|= ⟨t^{2} + 2t, 8, 2t^{3}⟩$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b40cf7a-fa7c-5050-b2e9-e2f7ba04828a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259977} {:answer/id #uuid "175264bb-f389-5869-951c-76cc68611d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260079} {:answer/id #uuid "214e0a46-a997-57f6-8fa7-46beb9676f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260159} {:answer/id #uuid "395164b8-31dd-524a-ab0d-565231ea5e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260386} {:answer/id #uuid "fce4134e-0fcd-5135-8ad0-7457cadd83ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "214e0a46-a997-57f6-8fa7-46beb9676f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260159} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eac5ff3-a989-52ce-a1dc-128ad336dc00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65ab200e-3546-5bdf-91aa-8c6105b3b769" :question/math-academy-id "q-128137" :question/problem "Find the value of $(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}$ at $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{3(t+1)},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-3{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3(t+1)}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(0)-3g(0))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(0)-3{g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+1}},\\,3(0)^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{0+1}⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3(0+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3},1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e9deaa-32e1-5ea1-8ac9-d0b7cec610d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260804} {:answer/id #uuid "786ded6e-e2cc-5b48-8f31-f18de453ddf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260928} {:answer/id #uuid "925c6509-691b-597c-8503-36e96b674fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261146} {:answer/id #uuid "bee221f3-f2b6-59f9-bc02-f014daed57c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\pi ,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261564} {:answer/id #uuid "e98af580-cfca-5b9f-a49f-53c6b11bb2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,4\\pi ,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "925c6509-691b-597c-8503-36e96b674fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261146} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f0cbd8-ad26-5506-89ef-79e23f60a2f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262130}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d61cd968-7256-5d6b-88d3-edf46ce0ae3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128452" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}$ at $t=-1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨8\\sqrt{3-t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,\\pi {t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)-{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8\\sqrt{3-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-t}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-1,\\,2\\pi t,\\,-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(-1)-g(-1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(-1)-{g}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-(-1)}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi ),\\,\\frac{1}{(-1)}⟩-⟨2(-1)-1,\\,2\\pi (-1),\\,-2(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨-2,-\\pi ,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2\\pi ,-2⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f2fbae0-f6d7-546c-827c-374938408879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260853} {:answer/id #uuid "71402034-ff9c-5e89-8506-730d8d44e9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260867} {:answer/id #uuid "92984806-47e0-5523-b871-7b33717a7972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261148} {:answer/id #uuid "d34e1c49-8247-5b18-a5d2-f237fc07b65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261733} {:answer/id #uuid "fc50c87f-1bce-55e7-87f1-cf2d24533ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d34e1c49-8247-5b18-a5d2-f237fc07b65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261733} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a5d268-0bb4-5a51-b597-b06cd810f718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262395}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "143a675a-6cf0-552b-b195-46b4f34bf0d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128458" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3+t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t-3 \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ (t+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have \n \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+5{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(2\\sqrt{3+t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+t}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1)^{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 2(t+1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence , we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(1)+5g(1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(1)+5{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(1) \\\\ 2(1+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ef80ee-161a-5a7e-8232-8f11f4ab0591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299960} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6f401a-1af1-5902-8ecf-8f185e9e12da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300092} {:answer/id #uuid "3d489b9a-c7ce-5bb5-9c1e-bb2fb01f89fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300261} {:answer/id #uuid "7630cb27-95dd-503c-86cf-d9a96b47156b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300546} {:answer/id #uuid "875ea830-aed4-554d-85ae-d63a3f76be32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ef80ee-161a-5a7e-8232-8f11f4ab0591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299960} :answer-field/id #uuid "610d999b-36f3-554e-acdc-7690f0627a2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301538}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ce8c747-438b-5a4a-8cfe-ec69b8a216ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-32499" :question/problem "Differentiate $2g(t)-h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t-3,\\,-{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-t,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have\n\n$$\n(2g(t)-h(t))^{′}=2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2g(t)-h(t))^{′} & =2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6-(-1),\\,-4t-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31df8d49-ce69-5cb1-a2cd-57e59e1196c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300209} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2a4bfc-5f35-5ae9-a821-d3bce3a9c6c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300442} {:answer/id #uuid "7a714d86-ceb0-57c7-a902-31a1b72e5f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300565} {:answer/id #uuid "87911319-25bb-5038-bd99-46da453974fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300646} {:answer/id #uuid "9e03f1e2-6fb5-5862-a16d-73e44a1f2e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31df8d49-ce69-5cb1-a2cd-57e59e1196c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300209} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4e2c0bf-91fb-53b7-a114-172b95036f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f67b45fc-cd86-5ee0-8299-de9e4060f565" :question/math-academy-id "q-32503" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41126a54-8e43-5888-909a-644b0fa2584e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302866} {:answer/id #uuid "89b704e5-d1d6-5b5f-b7c9-5e1091541afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303316} {:answer/id #uuid "989a417c-9f9c-520c-a1ca-b762a6d26b64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303404} {:answer/id #uuid "a7aa4261-f293-5497-8bca-0be34ef4c95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303485} {:answer/id #uuid "e704354b-3077-58df-9da8-1fc39413f08b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e704354b-3077-58df-9da8-1fc39413f08b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303892} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb6aef3-3384-522e-8f0d-b00fdf0b7619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304762}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3147421-0af0-52d2-8626-d7432dc16238" :question/math-academy-id "q-33123" :question/problem "Differentiate $2f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,(j-\\,k) \\\\ g(t) & =(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}1\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)+3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac5b001-3222-5f20-9cfa-a6a178edbcf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,16{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336134} {:answer/id #uuid "43211d42-ef9b-5294-9784-f61afc4354fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t},\\,2{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336665} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0b1790-c755-5de3-8e68-28d3776dc12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336737} {:answer/id #uuid "adc3c998-c9bf-5aa6-bbfb-3bb4b5b897c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337591} {:answer/id #uuid "d10a81b8-09d6-54a4-86e1-fa3b6c978c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d10a81b8-09d6-54a4-86e1-fa3b6c978c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337863} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6a4498-4274-5a8f-a340-b4c6887cef4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338409}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bba82f4d-eee0-52ff-96d4-e8a4604b03f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70681" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+4g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+4g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+4g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+4⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+⟨4,\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+4,\\,\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,0+16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a768cdba-762c-56fa-9c5a-e7c147a0278c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387861} {:answer/id #uuid "308ec3e7-64ed-53d8-95f6-4019058929dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387862} {:answer/id #uuid "c6683669-2c03-5f5d-9b0c-ade45ed8142d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387863} {:answer/id #uuid "76309ab8-5db5-5655-9fd2-0aa6a5daad69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387864} {:answer/id #uuid "3051e681-37d6-5351-a17b-b57925e0ca74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3051e681-37d6-5351-a17b-b57925e0ca74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387865} :answer-field/id #uuid "437f6985-a5fd-5604-8d5e-718379fa984b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387860}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e49dfe3-04a3-591e-9ea0-48737f115840" :question/math-academy-id "q-127998" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a16c9dc1-0124-53fd-9b82-d496e53dbcff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387868} {:answer/id #uuid "f616ca61-be0f-5144-b6c8-08476269dd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387869} {:answer/id #uuid "309785b0-a118-5c93-829d-4b1bec8533d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,7,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387870} {:answer/id #uuid "a99725fb-c5ed-5e02-9f65-da1970e78632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,7,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387871} {:answer/id #uuid "69eaec62-e0f1-50fe-ae12-fb1a693cb8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69eaec62-e0f1-50fe-ae12-fb1a693cb8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387872} :answer-field/id #uuid "f682f616-b62a-5bba-8f73-0577cd6f697d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387867}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "998ff16d-b6a6-5973-8b01-9ee14eef7c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-128144" :question/problem "Find the value of $(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-2{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(1)-2g(1))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(1)-2{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =⟨2(1),\\,\\frac{1}{1},\\,{e}^{1-1}⟩-2⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}},\\,3(1)^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-2⟨1,3,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115391 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114971 :question/id #uuid "3668609c-7f98-53ef-8aa7-6f9c3209dfee" :question/math-academy-id "e-2478" :question/problem "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where ![](images/9e/9e23d542bfc56d506f5437a35a92c304d618109ef60086e1f5a7a4fee57d8a80.png) and $u(t) = t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048813 :topic/math-academy-id 1109 :topic/title "The Product Rule for Differentiation"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115760 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab8d5ef-8089-5175-ac19-96485f970f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299985} {:answer/id #uuid "2593ced8-b033-50da-a809-fe4246142ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}-t \\\\ {5}^{t}+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300141} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2fd8d0-a070-5db6-ae81-ced05e60caa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300253} {:answer/id #uuid "a6872ccd-6c7e-5432-936d-73672be13108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 12{t}^{2}+36 \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300801} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb0c90f-dfca-51d0-b238-6b2f8dccaca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbb0c90f-dfca-51d0-b238-6b2f8dccaca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300980} :answer-field/id #uuid "0034e2a3-f8d6-5a9e-9977-de07c87e0df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301231}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39b28ff1-22a5-53af-8f2d-4d751a5c5d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-32286" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({5}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+2t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2{t}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af26b52e-3810-51ea-bcac-9c8acc178d2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15t^{4}, 9t^{2} - 4t^{3}, 12t^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113575} {:answer/id #uuid "d89a1010-b029-5792-8386-b98d376ee90c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6t^{4},-t^{3}, 3t^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113576} {:answer/id #uuid "0f6e6b35-ffb9-5f32-bb19-61dd743fdab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6t,-1, 3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113577} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca95614-cc13-54c2-bac6-53445010da41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3t^{2}, 3 - t, 3t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113578} {:answer/id #uuid "671b1663-a607-5e69-8ffb-86c468627dae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5t^{4}, 3t^{2}, 4t^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113579}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c2951b-1c72-5268-832b-3b8119eb6b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113574}] :question/id #uuid "e833221c-734a-52a6-a325-a894171df700" :question/math-academy-id "q-32501" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t) = ⟨3t^{2}, 3 - t, 3t⟩$ and $u(t) = t^{3}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f72b45b-32fa-5846-8f1b-fc09e15dd9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260433} {:answer/id #uuid "77fb7a60-00b8-5218-9921-1f39feba326a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260924} {:answer/id #uuid "8d76152a-5288-544b-8dea-d4af8e174c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261113} {:answer/id #uuid "9d391b58-7274-5c35-8b7b-6c8acc0893a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261234} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e6e1bb-d01a-512c-97e8-610afd3f35d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6e6e1bb-d01a-512c-97e8-610afd3f35d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262034} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8f8745-4998-5897-9f4a-16c888b2f208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262367}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "345451d2-c71d-53b2-ba4b-9528a0f7f324" :question/math-academy-id "q-128473" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bb14e6-4804-566e-8ba1-cd6661d9e27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259955} {:answer/id #uuid "42ea72dd-3fe1-52af-a8c1-ff45b339f5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2},\\,5\\sqrt{t},\\,3{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260458} {:answer/id #uuid "a0962aa2-e4c4-5ed5-a38d-661cd0c6397f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261270} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b920ba-40d7-52c4-8b7d-9ba1225aab16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261273} {:answer/id #uuid "b0145eca-83e8-5b7f-93f4-8603d5621461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,2t\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08bb14e6-4804-566e-8ba1-cd6661d9e27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259955} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f997dd1-3807-549f-be54-0c6c67a6ae0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262410}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f6ebbf1-7ac8-5d1e-b90d-f43ce0433207" :question/math-academy-id "q-128477" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $u(t)=2\\sqrt{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{t}⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4t\\sqrt{t},\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩+⟨1,\\,t\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f663231-0ba7-5629-be71-2d2ead4d3723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-2,\\,-t,\\,t-2{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260431} {:answer/id #uuid "586b07f8-82bd-52eb-bdf1-cf3065aede5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+t,\\,2+t,\\,t+3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260631} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa8b05a-0de5-5531-8860-7f42d89a207b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2t,\\,-1,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260700} {:answer/id #uuid "97d18fc2-232e-5625-a79a-3bb31bd8b790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2t,\\,-2t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261191} {:answer/id #uuid "d02647d8-a2fc-5aa9-bdb0-fd91b0c9215c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t,\\,-2{t}^{2},\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97d18fc2-232e-5625-a79a-3bb31bd8b790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2t,\\,-2t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261191} :answer-field/id #uuid "151308c3-28fc-5bd3-ab19-c0fac585d178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262161}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28487445-4637-5ffc-a325-dcbc682a33b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128479" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨t,\\,1+t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=1-t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =(1-t)⟨1,\\,1,\\,2t⟩-⟨t,\\,1+t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-t,\\,1-t,\\,2t-2{t}^{2}⟩-⟨t,\\,1+t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2t,\\,-2t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff800d3-9925-5a1f-9bfc-6f9a48992b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3}+2t,\\,4{t}^{2}+6{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260023} {:answer/id #uuid "29455431-af0d-5c43-a32c-24a26aa144f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260237} {:answer/id #uuid "311ab69a-928a-588d-9516-989f0c7c8e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260316} {:answer/id #uuid "7d8672a2-39a1-59bb-bc5c-8f90cd8fffd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260968} {:answer/id #uuid "93a8bad7-ecb6-5eb1-b599-4e63c3bbc5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "311ab69a-928a-588d-9516-989f0c7c8e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260316} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68cb0b5-e8bb-527b-ae06-1c4fc55256df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c82af0d-c66c-5c8e-bb72-c5cfe1d3d608" :question/math-academy-id "q-128481" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩+2⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,6{t}^{3},\\,2t+4{t}^{2}⟩+⟨8\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,2t+2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a95b330-bb37-5112-b358-d912678bfc92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-t},\\,2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260400} {:answer/id #uuid "3e40b650-d8f4-57b2-907a-ecc623553ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{-t},\\,1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260423} {:answer/id #uuid "584135ce-ff8c-5cfb-be88-d839ebd7fb66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,{t}^{2}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260627} {:answer/id #uuid "701fd60a-c439-5e95-8ef7-d416b3758579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260860} {:answer/id #uuid "91c2f62a-23b7-59f8-9406-a77293ea9045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-t,\\,2(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "701fd60a-c439-5e95-8ef7-d416b3758579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260860} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ba4514-1f97-55cf-8137-48dda5c44cce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b459a16-1ddd-5fd7-b65f-64ec230fc1a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128485" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨2{e}^{-t},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}⟨-2{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,0⟩+t⟨2{e}^{-t},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,2t,\\,0⟩+⟨2t{e}^{-t},\\,4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{-t}-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,2t+4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1e76c73-4dda-53f0-be01-314247fc0ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337755} {:answer/id #uuid "e205aafb-db03-50ba-a9cf-e2e2bf49b182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337999} {:answer/id #uuid "ecde76ee-f28d-580d-9db5-9149c8cdbb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338099} {:answer/id #uuid "ed54e252-e227-5dc6-9931-79218dd313f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{3}+3t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338102} {:answer/id #uuid "fff0d9bc-2402-5c81-84fb-e6405699052c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e76c73-4dda-53f0-be01-314247fc0ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337755} :answer-field/id #uuid "936abeb3-90ac-5f81-aede-5e4550d7f9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338550}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f31a5c94-f740-5b67-b455-a131169207f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-70685" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ t \\\\ {t}^{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fe3261-4909-5096-b5e1-f76176162165" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336357} {:answer/id #uuid "712f0496-f2a0-5abd-b4c8-73de224a043e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337041} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8d1eff-3823-57a2-bdcc-d1c03822f1b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337176} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdbc4b9-9974-5b9e-acea-527268caf412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337700} {:answer/id #uuid "c8dacc4f-6a8e-538f-a3d3-2b9938bc01da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e8d1eff-3823-57a2-bdcc-d1c03822f1b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337176} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e58e48c-9dd0-5119-9cc7-b119ae414c42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338387}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "caf13fa2-de78-52bc-ba1b-170f27934a7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71225" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ae2bca-e693-5057-b172-8c6834c9305c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ -8t \\\\ -3t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336046} {:answer/id #uuid "3b032cb3-2592-5b9d-9061-33bfc2a7a76d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336587} {:answer/id #uuid "5f14825a-b07a-50fe-8e14-408159c0bd18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"